From b681c525a254c3c4eeab6a76193dabb66c82ea6d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: keptn42 <keptn42@noreply.codeberg.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 11:54:32 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] moe_gemm_q_mod4: the quantised grouped GEMM over four
 classes of experts

moe_gemm_q over four tables instead of two: expert e is entry e / 4 of class
e % 4. A separate op, because the declaration divides a table op's weights
over its table operands by count. The arguments are repacked to fit four
classes in 256 bytes; moe_gemm_q's arithmetic is unchanged. Where weights
do not divide evenly over the tables, the first tables take one more each
(510 experts: 128/128/127/127). libref and libavx serve the op.
